    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "Same misuse of `open` as F:godel-first-incompleteness, for the same reason. Recorded because it is the proposition that makes `unknown` a first-class result rather than a failure: this theorem is the reason axeyum's solver trait must be allowed to decline, and it is the boundary the whole 'ladder past quantifier-free' programme is climbing toward rather than through. Note the exact shape of the limit -- it forbids a decision procedure, not a semi-decision procedure. Validity in FOL is recursively enumerable, so a complete PROVER is possible and only a complete DECIDER is not, and that distinction is what separates a reachable goal from an impossible one for this repository. Formalising the statement would need the same reflection machinery F:godel-first-incompleteness names, plus a model of computation.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
